Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot Part 2

 Project Overview
This project is a WPF-based Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot developed in C#. The chatbot is designed to educate users about basic cybersecurity threats such as phishing, scams, password safety, and privacy protection.

The system uses a graphical user interface (GUI) to make interactions more user-friendly and includes voice output, memory recall, sentiment detection, and keyword recognition.



Features
 Keyword Recognition
The chatbot detects cybersecurity-related keywords such as:
- Password
- Scam
- Privacy
- Phishing

It responds with relevant cybersecurity advice based on the detected keyword.


 Random Responses
To make interactions more dynamic, the chatbot uses lists of predefined responses and randomly selects:
- Phishing tips
- Security warnings



 Memory and Recall
The chatbot remembers user information such as:
- User name
- User’s cybersecurity interest (e.g. privacy)

It uses this information later to personalise responses.

Example:
- “Nice to meet you Alex”
- “As someone interested in privacy, you should review your security settings.”



Sentiment Detection
The chatbot detects user emotions such as:
- Worried
- Curious
- Frustrated

It adjusts responses to be more empathetic and supportive when needed.


 Conversation Flow
The chatbot maintains context during conversations and supports follow-up inputs such as:
- “Tell me more”
- “Explain more”
- “Another tip”

This allows continuous conversation without restarting context.


Voice Implementation
The chatbot uses `System.Speech.Synthesis` to provide voice output for key responses, improving user engagement and interactivity.



 Error Handling
The chatbot includes default responses for unrecognised inputs to ensure stability:
- “I'm not sure I understand. Can you try rephrasing?”


 Technologies Used
- C#
- WPF (Windows Presentation Foundation)
- .NET Framework / .NET (with System.Speech via NuGet)
- Visual Studio



